[CENTER][SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]RespawnBlocks[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=5][I]Regenerating ores and blocks inside WorldGuard regions[/I][/SIZE]

[B]Minecraft 1.16.5 – 1.21.x[/B]  •  [B]Spigot & Paper[/B]  •  [B]Requires WorldGuard[/B][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]What is RespawnBlocks?[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
RespawnBlocks turns any WorldGuard region into a [B]regenerating mine[/B]. When a player mines an ore inside a respawn region, it turns into a placeholder block (bedrock by default). After a configurable time, the [B]original block comes back[/B]. Every block has its own timer.

Perfect for [B]mine islands, public mines, prison mines, skyblock/oneblock-style resource areas and resource worlds[/B].

Everything is managed from an [B]in-game GUI[/B]. No config editing needed, but every setting and every message can still be changed in the config files.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Per-block respawn timers[/B]: every block type has its own respawn time, placeholder and drop mode.
[*][B]Any block can respawn[/B]: all ores are set up by default (overworld, deepslate, copper, nether and ancient debris). You can add logs, stone or anything else.
[*][B]Exact restore[/B]: the original block comes back with its full block state.
[*][B]Chunk-safe[/B]: never force-loads chunks. Blocks in unloaded chunks respawn the moment their chunk loads again.
[*][B]Restart- and crash-safe[/B]: waiting blocks are saved to disk, so no stray bedrock is left behind after a restart. Downtime counts towards the timer.
[*][B]Vanilla mining[/B]: Fortune, Silk Touch, tool durability, XP and Mending all work. Plugins like jobs and mcMMO see a normal block break.
[*][B]3 drop modes[/B]: drops on the ground, drops straight into the inventory, or the block itself (classic MineIsland style).
[*][B]WorldGuard integration[/B]: mine respawn blocks even in regions with [I]build deny[/I], while all other blocks stay protected.
[*][B]Placeholder protection[/B]: explosions, pistons, fire and mobs can't remove placeholders.
[*][B]Full GUI[/B]: add blocks, change times and placeholders, and enable or disable regions per world.
[*][B]Tab completion[/B] for every command, including your WorldGuard regions and all block names.
[*][B]Fully translatable[/B]: prefix, messages and all GUI texts, with & color codes and hex colors ([I]&#RRGGBB[/I]).
[*][B]Respawn effects[/B]: configurable sound and block particles.
[*][B]Lightweight[/B]: one region lookup per block break and no async trickery. Works with Spigot, Paper, Purpur and other forks.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]The GUI[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Open it with [B]/rb gui[/B].
[LIST]
[*][B]Blocks menu[/B]: see all respawn blocks with their time, placeholder and drop mode. [I]Click a block in your own inventory to add it.[/I]
[*][B]Block editor[/B]:
[LIST]
[*]Change the respawn time with -60 / -10 / -1 / +1 / +10 / +60 second buttons.
[*]Set a placeholder by clicking a block in your inventory.
[*]Switch the drop mode, enable or disable the block, or remove it.
[/LIST]
[*][B]Regions menu[/B]: lists every WorldGuard region per world.
[LIST]
[*]Click a region to make it a respawn region, and click again to enable or disable it.
[*]Switch between worlds, and filter on respawn regions only.
[/LIST]
[*][B]Main menu[/B]: turn the whole plugin on or off, respawn all waiting blocks instantly, and reload.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]Requirements[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Spigot or Paper (or a fork), [B]1.16.5 up to the latest version[/B]
[*][URL='https://dev.bukkit.org/projects/worldguard']WorldGuard 7.x[/URL] (pick the version that matches your server)
[*][URL='https://dev.bukkit.org/projects/worldedit']WorldEdit[/URL] or FastAsyncWorldEdit (needed by WorldGuard)
[/LIST]
[B]One single jar for all versions.[/B] Blocks that don't exist on older versions (like deepslate ores on 1.16) are skipped automatically.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]Installation[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Install WorldEdit (or FAWE) and WorldGuard.
[*]Drop [B]RespawnBlocks.jar[/B] into your [I]plugins[/I] folder and restart the server.
[*]Create a WorldGuard region around your mine: [I]/rg define mine[/I]
[*]Mark it as respawn region: [I]/rb region add mine[/I] (or click it in [I]/rb gui[/I]).
[*]Done! Ores mined in that region now regenerate.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]Commands[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Main command [B]/respawnblocks[/B]. Aliases: [B]/rb[/B] and [B]/mineisland[/B].
[LIST]
[*][B]/rb gui[/B]: open the management GUI
[*][B]/rb region add|remove|toggle <region> [world][/B]: manage respawn regions
[*][B]/rb region list [world][/B]: list respawn regions
[*][B]/rb block add <block|hand> [seconds][/B]: add a respawn block
[*][B]/rb block remove <block>[/B]: remove a respawn block
[*][B]/rb block settime <block> <seconds>[/B]: change a respawn time
[*][B]/rb block list[/B]: list respawn blocks
[*][B]/rb respawnall [region][/B]: respawn all waiting blocks right now
[*][B]/rb toggle[/B]: turn the plugin on or off
[*][B]/rb reload[/B]: reload all configuration files
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#8b5cf6]Permissions[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]respawnblocks.admin[/B]: all commands and the GUI (default: op)
[*][B]respawnblocks.reload[/B]: only /rb reload (default: op)
[*][B]respawnblocks.bypass[/B]: break any block in respawn regions. In creative mode, also remove placeholders (default: op)
[/LIST]
Players need [B]no permission[/B] to mine respawn blocks.

